{"q":"416","t":"Partition Equal Subset Sum","d":"Medium","p":false,"c":"<p>Given an integer array <code>nums</code>, return <code>true</code> <em>if you can partition the array into two subsets such that the sum of the elements in both subsets is equal or </em><code>false</code><em> otherwise</em>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> nums = [1,5,11,5]\n<strong>Output:</strong> true\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> The array can be partitioned as [1, 5, 5] and [11].\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> nums = [1,2,3,5]\n<strong>Output:</strong> false\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> The array cannot be partitioned into equal sum subsets.\n</pre>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= nums.length &lt;= 200</code></li>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= nums[i] &lt;= 100</code></li>\n</ul>\n","h":[],"m":"{\r\n  \"name\": \"canPartition\",\r\n  \"params\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"nums\",\r\n      \"type\": \"integer[]\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"return\": {\r\n    \"type\": \"boolean\"\r\n  }\r\n}","g":[{"name":"Array","slug":"array"},{"name":"Dynamic Programming","slug":"dynamic-programming"},{"name":"Knapsack Problem","slug":"knapsack-problem"},{"name":"0-1 Knapsack","slug":"0-1-knapsack"}],"s":[{"t":"Partition to K Equal Sum Subsets","s":"partition-to-k-equal-sum-subsets","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Minimize the Difference Between Target and Chosen Elements","s":"minimize-the-difference-between-target-and-chosen-elements","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Maximum Number of Ways to Partition an Array","s":"maximum-number-of-ways-to-partition-an-array","d":"Hard","p":false},{"t":"Partition Array Into Two Arrays to Minimize Sum Difference","s":"partition-array-into-two-arrays-to-minimize-sum-difference","d":"Hard","p":false},{"t":"Find Subarrays With Equal Sum","s":"find-subarrays-with-equal-sum","d":"Easy",